fund-js/14-iterators-and-generators/01-l.solution:
export function* chunks(iterable, size) {
  if (!Number.isInteger(size) || size < 1) throw new RangeError('size must be a whole number of 1 or more');
  let batch = [];
  for (const item of iterable) {
    batch.push(item);
    if (batch.length === size) {
      yield batch;
      batch = [];
    }
  }
  if (batch.length > 0) yield batch;
}

fund-js/14-iterators-and-generators/01-l.explanation:
Accumulate into a batch and yield it whenever it is full; flush the remainder at the end:

```js
let batch = [];
for (const item of iterable) {
  batch.push(item);
  if (batch.length === size) { yield batch; batch = []; }
}
if (batch.length > 0) yield batch;
```

Because the `for...of` sits inside the generator, each `next()` pulls just enough items for one chunk. `Array.from(iterable)` first would hang on an infinite source and fail the "pulls only" test.
